cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these models, please cite the version you used."
title: "tujia-asr: released acoustic models for syllable-level Tujia speech recognition"
abstract: >-
  Syllable-level CTC acoustic models for Tujia speech recognition, built on
  wav2vec2-xlsr-53-espeak with a BiLSTM CTC head. v0.1 emits toneless syllable
  shapes; v0.2 and v0.3 emit toned syllables; v0.4 uses a 932-class toneless head
  plus a separate four-tone head. Code is MIT-licensed; weights and the fine-tuned
  encoder are released for research use only, and the training corpus is not
  distributed.
authors:
  - name: "ibaibing"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibaibing/tujia-asr"
keywords:
  - Tujia
  - speech recognition
  - low-resource languages
  - CTC
  - tone
  - wav2vec2
